BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Downtown Mystic Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTSTAMP:20261025T144727Z
UID:84b25dc48e9bfb13f9ce1fcdc754@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Our Original Ghost Walk takes travelers through the historic d
 owntown Mystic landscape crossing the bascule bridge between both sides of
  the Mystic River\, guests will become immersed in the dark\, sordid and s
 upernatural history of New England’s famous seafaring village. From 17th
  century strife of colonial life amidst the Pequot Wars and the King Phill
 ip’s war to mysterious turn of the century murders\, Mystic’s history 
 was founded in darkness. As the centuries grew\, lost seafarers\, creepy c
 ryptids\, and scandalous happenings took place in our quaint seaside commu
 nity.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Liberty Pole Square\, East Main Street\, Holmes Street\, Mystic C
 T\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirits of Mystic Pub Crawl
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTSTAMP:20261025T144727Z
UID:d2055bf0b2e3ceda180fb850dad2@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Raise a glass to the past and sip your way through Mystic’s 
 haunted history on the Spirits of Mystic Pub Crawl! Join Seaside Shadows f
 or a thrilling evening where ghostly legends and local libations collide. 
 As you stroll through Mystic’s historic streets\, you’ll hear chilling
  tales of spirits that still linger in centuries-old buildings\, from eeri
 e maritime mysteries to haunted taverns where the past refuses to rest.\n
 \nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/spirits-mystic-pub-crawl-0
LOCATION:Bank Square\, Water Street\, West Main Street\, Mystic CT\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/spirits-mystic-pub-crawl-0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moonlit Mystic Graveyard Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTSTAMP:20261025T144727Z
UID:87cc9db5307d7b0277c324c812fb@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:There’s nothing more intimately haunting than a colonial bur
 ial ground and Mystic boasts some of the most fascinating and haunted buri
 al grounds around. The Graveyard Ghost tour takes place at Whitehall Buria
 l Ground just off Hendel Drive in Mystic. Whitehall Burial Ground establis
 hed in the 1660’s was one of the common burial places of Mystic until th
 e rural landscape movement arrived to Mystic in 1854. Our Graveyard Ghost 
 Tour tells tales of some of Mystic’s most famous residents.\n\nSource: h
 ttps://ctvisit.com/events/moonlit-mystic-graveyard-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Hendel Drive\, Mystic CT\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/moonlit-mystic-graveyard-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dudley Farm Farmers Market & More
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTSTAMP:20261025T144727Z
UID:e342764ac12210955a536489f043@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Dudley Farm continues the old-time practice of selling produce
  at a roadside stand and is one of the oldest farmers markets in Connectic
 ut. Our Saturday morning market brings the community together on the site 
 of a living museum. Come purchase your produce\, home-baked goods and hand
 crafts\; bring your children to visit the livestock and romp on the hillsi
 de\; explore new exhibits in the Farmhouse and Dawnland museums. Throughou
 t the season we’ll have special workshops\, demonstrations and music. Co
 me wander our grounds with a hot cup of coffee and fresh muffin.\n\nSource
 : https://ctvisit.com/events/dudley-farm-farmers-market-more
LOCATION:Dudley Farm\, 2351 Durham Road\, Guilford CT\, 06437
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/dudley-farm-farmers-market-more
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norwich Stories of the American Revolution
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280101
DTSTAMP:20261025T144727Z
UID:c5d13aef0c36e1820a30a1a8eed9@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Norwich\, Connecticut was a center of Revolutionary activity i
 n Eastern Connecticut. From bands of Sons of Liberty to dedicated soldiers
  of all backgrounds\, the city produced scores of men and women who served
  in all capacities. From humble militiamen to a Signer of the Declaration 
 of Independence\, come and learn the lesser-known stories of these valiant
  Patriots as well as the story of America’s most infamous traitor\, Bene
 dict Arnold.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-america
 n-revolution
LOCATION:Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\, Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sharks Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20261025T144727Z
UID:e900bdd06c9878548021b8ca7c6d@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:People have been fascinated by sharks for as long as we have e
 xplored the ocean\, and now the Connecticut Science Center is bringing tha
 t fascination to life in the limited-time exhibition\, Sharks. This immers
 ive experience brings you face-to-face with some of the ocean’s most fas
 cinating predators through full-scale shark models\, interactive experienc
 es\, underwater environments\, ancient fossils\, immersive media\, and —
  of course — a lot of teeth.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/shark
 s-exhibition
LOCATION:Connecticut Science Center\, 250 Columbus Boulevard\, Hartford CT
 \, 06103
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/sharks-exhibition
END:VEVENT
